  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse multisectorielle aux inondations dans les provinces de N&#x2019;Djam&#xE9;na, du Logone Occidental et du Mandoul</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this $1.8m UNICEF project is to provide a multisectoral flood response in the education, WASH and shelter sectors. To that end UNICEF will provide 26,000 flood-affected Chadians in Logone Occidental and Mandoul with shelter kits, provide 24,000 people in N&#x2019;Djamena with cash transfers for shelter, construct 300 latrines, distribute essential WASH items to 50,000 people, construct or rehabilitate water points serving 7,500 people, rehabilitate 5 temporary learning centers, distribute school materials to 44,112 children and 735 teachers. In total, UNICEF will target 50,000 people through the WASH and shelter/NFI activities, including 10,400 women and 15,600 girls, and 44,112 children through education activities. Among those targeted UNICEF expects to be 7,500 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
